MLD6QUERY(8)              BSD System Manager's Manual             MLD6QUERY(8)

NNAAMMEE
     mmlldd66qquueerryy — send multicast listener query

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmlldd66qquueerryy [--ddggrr] _i_n_t_f_a_c_e [_m_a_d_d_r]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmlldd66qquueerryy utility sends an IPv6 multicast listener discovery (MLD)
     query packet toward the specified multicast address, _m_a_d_d_r, toward inter‐
     face _i_n_t_f_a_c_e.  If you omit _m_a_d_d_r, linklocal all nodes multicast ad‐
     dress(ff02::1) is used.

     After sending a query, mmlldd66qquueerryy waits for replies for at most 10 sec‐
     onds.  If a reply is returned, mmlldd66qquueerryy prints it with its type and then
     waits for another reply.

     This program is provided only for debugging.  It is not necessary for
     normal use.

     With --gg, mmlldd66qquueerryy will transmit a General Query instead of the default
     Multicast-Address-Specific Query.  With --dd, mmlldd66qquueerryy will transmit MLD
     done packet instead of MLD query packet.  With --rr, similarly, MLD report
     packet will be transmitted.  --ddrr options are for debugging purposes only.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The program exits with 0 on success, non-zero on failures.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The mmlldd66qquueerryy utility first appeared in WIDE/KAME IPv6 protocol stack
     kit.

BBUUGGSS
     The mmlldd66qquueerryy utility does not take care of multicast addresses which
     have non link-local scope.

